  "spec": "Track D, adaptation against alignment, with the control cl_fwriter asked for at 04:41Z (a single foreign specialist understates alignment because it also carries negative transfer). Same ten contexts, random slots, the same four views for every column, in-corpus init (fleet_M_x2 valley_002). Columns: ctxr = fine-tuned on the context's OWN SEARCH rows (2,000 exposures per row, the runs of ledger line 29); lofo = a leave-own-family-out generalist: one fine-tune per context on evaluation-matched episodes of the SEARCH rows of the OTHER nine contexts of pool ctx_pool_v1, equal weight per table, with the same optimisation budget as one own-table run (222 exposures per row on each of nine tables, about the same optimiser steps and query exposures in total as 2,000 on one), same recipe otherwise (peak LR 5e-5, stage c9c8b9c95e; runs ctx_tts/runs/g1_lofo_<family>_rand); forr = the single foreign specialist of ledger line 30; init = the pre-fine-tune checkpoint. Baseline lofo_mean3, so the paired reads are ctxr minus lofo (ADAPTATION to the table), init minus lofo (minus ALIGNMENT with the evaluation pipeline) and forr minus lofo. Registered before any of the twenty fine-tunes exists and before lines 25 and 26 were scored. READING RULE, fixed now, counts over the ten contexts with family-mean sign: (A) adaptation holds if ctxr beats lofo on at least 7 of 10 with a positive mean difference; (B) alignment holds if lofo beats init on at least 7 of 10 with a positive mean difference. A and not B: per-table fine-tuning (S4 arm B4) stays the pick. B and not A: B4 is dropped and the pick moves to one generalist trained on evaluation-matched episodes. A and B: both are real; the generalist comes first because it is free at inference, and B4 is tested on top of it at stack level. Neither: the fresh-row gain of the family specialists is not reproduced from SEARCH rows by either route and the pick is withdrawn. This rule replaces the one in line 30 for the decision; line 30 stays as the worst-case transfer read. Prediction: B holds (lofo beats init on 7 or more); ctxr beats lofo on 5 to 7 of 10 with a mean difference between -0.02 and +0.10 u, so I expect \"B and not A\" or a narrow \"A and B\". Descriptive in the statistical sense: ten contexts, one seed, the smallest two-sided sign-flip p is 0.002; it selects no arm for a dev91 look.",
